MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The step drill bits and carbide burrs fit the work suggested by my rivets, rivet nuts and drill bits: making mounting holes, then cleaning up their edges. I'd check the burrs fit my tool before buying.",
    "The small stainless screws and metric countersunk screws extend my fastening supplies, while the waterproof tape offers a sealing function beyond the mounting tapes I already have."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The copper pipe brush and motor capacitor require specific jobs I haven't identified. Buying repair tools doesn't mean I currently need plumbing supplies or a replacement motor component.",
    "The crowd-control ropes and bakery boxes don't help with my current drilling, fastening, fabrication or repair projects."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations seem to treat broadly related workshop and maintenance supplies as interchangeable, even when they serve very different tasks.",
    "Matching a thread size is only part of finding useful hardware: the three-inch screws could fit some of my rivet nuts, but I don't have a project that needs that length."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated purchases of rivets, rivet nuts, bolts and drilling tools make accessories for preparing holes and assembling parts especially relevant right now.",
    "I often buy versatile assortments and reusable tools. A specialized part needs a known job and matching specifications before I'd choose it."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly understood my fastening and fabrication work, but stretched that interest into specialized repairs and unrelated supplies without a clear project connection."
}
